  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1108 PM CDT Sat Sep 26 2026\n\nRidging will continue to build into the area by the middle of the\nweek, pushing temperatures back up into the upper 80s to low 90s. \nSoutherly flow will return during the time, unfortunately bringing\nhigher humidity back. A large trough will develop out west near \nthe end of the week, but uncertainty remains in its eventual path \nand how quickly it will move. On the whole, things will remain dry\nthrough at least Friday with low to medium rain chances returning\nto the forecast this weekend. For those keeping up, if we finish \nthe month of September without another drop of rain in Nashville, \nthis will be the first time since October of 1963 that BNA has \nmeasured a trace or less or precipitation for an entire month. \nNeedless to say, some rain would be great, but the pattern is not \nin favor of it right now.",
